course: dictionary
lesson: 14543
title: Perturbation: worry or a small disturbance
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Perturbation is a noun, so it names a thing or feeling. Its everyday meaning is worry or being upset. «Mum noticed a perturbation in Sam's voice when he said the test was tomorrow.» Sam's voice showed he was worried.
explain: In science, a perturbation is a small change or disturbance in how something moves. «Jupiter's pull caused a small perturbation in the orbit of the comet.» The comet's path was nudged a little off its usual track. Astronomers used this idea to find Neptune in 1846, after they noticed small disturbances in Uranus's orbit.
fact: Perturbation means worry or anxiety, or being upset.
fact: In science, a perturbation is a small change or disturbance in movement, such as a planet's orbit being pulled by another planet.
fact: «Perturbation» is a noun: one perturbation, two perturbations.
fact: Astronomers noticed small perturbations in Uranus's orbit, and this helped them discover Neptune in 1846.
fact: To work out which meaning fits, ask: is the sentence about a feeling (worry) or about movement (a small push or change)?
exercise: «Jamal felt a perturbation of worry when the lights went out.» What does perturbation mean here? | *Worry or upset | Joy at a party | A very quick run | A large, sunny garden
exercise: «The moon's pull made a small perturbation in the satellite's path.» What does perturbation mean here? | A perfect, unchanging circle | *A small change in movement | Loud noise from the sky | A new name for a planet
exercise: Which word means a small disturbance in how something moves? | Silence | Brightness | Calm | *Perturbation
test: «Mum saw a perturbation on her son's face before the trip.» What does perturbation suggest? | Sleepiness | Hunger | *Worry | Laughter
test: Astronomers used small perturbations in Uranus's orbit to find which planet? | Saturn | Venus | *Neptune | Mars
exam: «The ship's course showed a slight perturbation after the storm.» What does perturbation mean here? | A bright new colour on the deck | Sailors singing happily | Ship's engine failing completely | *A small change or disturbance in the ship's movement
